A||||6||mrfiero||How fast was I going?||||6||
Z||000000||mrfiero||11-04-2001||06:09 PM||||Just curious if anyone out there knows how to calculate speed based on RPM's & gear ratios.  <P>I had the GT wound up the other day (needle pegged past 120MPH) and was trying to figure out exactly how fast I was going.  <P>I had it at 4500 RPM's in 5th gear....this is a 3.61 Getrag. The wheels are stock as  are the tire sizes (215/60-15 rear).<P>I think the tach even reads a bit on the low side, so the RPM's may have been a little higher than 4500, but I'm not sure.<P>Anyone know how to figure this out?  Do I need more info.?  Any help would be appreciated (as in a mathematical formula).<P>I'm guessing it was around 130MPH, but I want to know for sure.....it felt faster than the 120MPH the speedo was reading (don't ask me how I know this.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">) <P>Thanks.||||reg||6
Z||000001||Old Lar||11-04-2001||06:35 PM||||Mikey you are a bad boy.  For a rough calculation I assume a linear relationship between rpm and mph.  MY 5 speed I run ~2400 rpm at 70 mph in 5th gear.  Using that ratio, how fast would I be going at 4500 rpm?  Calculates out to 131 mph.  I think the linearity starts falling off but I don't think I have the HP to get up to 4500 in 5th gear. (I got to 4200 rpm once) Not too many good clear staight aways in this part of the country.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||11-04-2001||08:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Old Lar:<BR><B>Mikey you are a bad boy.  For a rough calculation I assume a linear relationship between rpm and mph.  MY 5 speed I run ~2400 rpm at 70 mph in 5th gear.  Using that ratio, how fast would I be going at 4500 rpm?  Calculates out to 131 mph.  I think the linearity starts falling off but I don't think I have the HP to get up to 4500 in 5th gear. (I got to 4200 rpm once) Not too many good clear staight aways in this part of the country.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks Larry.  I was using my "seat-o-pants meter" and it felt like 130, so I was flying!<P>We have quite a few long stretches of desolate road out here, so stretching the legs on your car is pretty easy to do.  <P>The GT seems to be a bit slower accelerating than most of my previous Fieros, but once it's up to speed it flies.   <P><BR>***disclaimer***<P>I guess I should state that I don't advocate speeding or reckless driving, but if the road is open and your car is up to snuff go for it (just don't blame me if you get caught.....I'll deny everything!)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>BTW......the headlight doors didn't pop up until I started decelerating.  I thought that was a little odd.<P>Thanks again.||||reg||10
Z||000003||Jefrysuko||11-04-2001||09:11 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrfiero:<BR><B>BTW......the headlight doors didn't pop up until I started decelerating.  I thought that was a little odd.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hmmm... The car will squat a little on deceleration if you were using the engine only (not the brakes) the rear might have squatted a little more than the front.  Or you might have hit a bump or a gust of wind.  It is interesting though.<P>I need to get out and get my headlight doors to pop up like that just so that I can say that I did it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||2birds||11-04-2001||09:38 PM||||I had my 5 speed 86 GT to 4500 RPM for a stretch on the Montanabahn a few years ago.  My wife was tailing me in the Supercoupe, and she said it was hovering around the 130 mark.  Windows up, sunroof out, no AC, and that was about all I could get out of it.<P>That was fun...||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfiero||11-04-2001||10:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jefrysuko:<BR><B> Hmmm... The car will squat a little on deceleration if you were using the engine only (not the brakes) the rear might have squatted a little more than the front.  Or you might have hit a bump or a gust of wind.  It is interesting though.<P>I need to get out and get my headlight doors to pop up like that just so that I can say that I did it   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>My GT is lowered too, so it squats even more than "normal".  I believe that a gust of wind hit me at the same time I was starting to lift off the throttle, but I was concentrating on what was ahead of me so I can't say for sure.  That makes sense though.<P>All I can say is the first time the doors fly open on you it scares the $*&# out of you!  Afterwards it is just plain annoying. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Huck||11-05-2001||12:14 AM||||You ever get it so that the doors aren't wide open, but aren't shut?  Kinda like they dont know what to do..  This happens quite frequently to me at about 100mph when you fly past a big truck... they open up, bob up and down a little... thats when I punch the brakes to shut them again, and then carry on!  Other times only one will open and do that... its like its  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> winking  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> at the people I pass...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Huck<BR>87 GT T-tops||||reg||1
